## Run
```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install ansible boto3 botocore
ansible-galaxy collection install -r collections/requirements.yml
aws configure                                   # credentials for {{ aws_region }}

ansible-playbook preflight.yml                  # checks creds + variables
ansible-playbook site.yml --check               # dry run
ansible-playbook site.yml                        # create bucket + distribution
```

## Publish your build
```bash
aws s3 sync ./dist/ s3://{{ bucket_name }}/      # upload the SPA build
```
The site is served at the CloudFront domain printed by `site.yml` (CDN
propagation takes a few minutes on first deploy).

> The bucket stays **private**; CloudFront reaches it via Origin Access. Add a
> custom domain + ACM certificate on the distribution for your own hostname.
